            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0235" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/1152: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-17T11:00:00-05:00">June 17, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs in an official communiqué today announces
                    that the Ecuadoran and Peruvian Governments have agreed to withdraw their
                    respective troops which were sent to the frontier since the incident of June 1
                    and to free the soldiers captured, at 9:00 o’clock this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
